From: Androlinzberg maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] libgui: adapt host caller identity, gralloc and EGL boundaries

Pinned AOSP producer interfaces retain their original Binder/HIDL discovery.
BufferQueueThreadState uses authenticated AZKB caller identity. Remove an unused
ComposerService include from BufferQueueCore.

Select host allocator/mapper factories at libui's Gralloc boundary. Retain the
stock GraphicBuffer validation, metadata, accounting and ownership above it;
the host backend owns GBM allocations and imported DMA-BUF descriptors.

GLConsumer imports DMA-BUF images through the shared host EGL seam. EGL
capability probes use the graphics device's GBM display. Explicit host display
references preserve AOSP's balanced image/probe lifetime over Mesa, whose
initialize/terminate calls do not implement Android's reference counting.

